_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_

**Approval endpoints are unauthenticated and allow caller spoofing.**

Line 221–263 accepts `{ user }` directly from request body and processes approvals/rejections without authn/authz checks. This can let an unauthenticated caller approve high-risk patches.


<details>
<summary>Proposed hardening (minimal)</summary>

```diff
 this.fastify.post('/approvals/:id/approve', async (request, reply) => {
   const { id } = request.params as { id: string };
-  const { user } = request.body as { user: string };
+  const { user } = request.body as { user: string };
+  const apiKey = request.headers['x-autopilot-api-key'];
+  if (!apiKey || apiKey !== process.env.AUTOPILOT_API_KEY) {
+    return reply.code(401).send({ error: 'Unauthorized' });
+  }
@@
-  const success = await this.approvalManager.approve(approval.repo, approval.pr, id, user);
+  const allowed = await this.approvalManager.canUserApprove(approval.repo, user, approval.pr);
+  if (!allowed) {
+    return reply.code(403).send({ error: 'Forbidden' });
+  }
+  const success = await this.approvalManager.approve(approval.repo, approval.pr, id, user);
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.

In `@scripts/agent.ts` around lines 176 - 263, The approval endpoints accept a
user from the request body and call approvalManager.approve/reject without
authentication, allowing caller spoofing; fix by enforcing authentication and
authorization: remove trust of the body "user" field in the POST handlers for
'/approvals/:id/approve' and '/approvals/:id/reject', require an authenticated
principal (e.g. populate request.user from your auth middleware/token), validate
that request.user.identity is allowed to approve/reject this approval (e.g.
compare to approval.requestedReviewers or check roles/permissions), and pass the
authenticated identity into approvalManager.approve and approvalManager.reject
instead of the user from the body; also validate/deny any request that lacks a
valid auth token or sufficient permission.
```

</details>

